    "created_at": "2018-06-08T07:55:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-08T07:55:27Z",
    "body": "So we'd need to define:\r\n\r\n- what a block is,\r\n- how to pass blocks an initial set of key/value pairs (variable name and value) which are declared in it,\r\n- that variables are accessible _by reference_ from nested steps or following steps (i.e. that variable declarations are not hoisted).\r\n\r\nA new block is created:\r\n\r\n1. implicitly every time a _desugared_ step is nested,\r\n1. explicitly, for certain constructs (e.g. loops).\r\n\r\nConditional statements which occur in the same step are—I think—the only ones which need to be \r\ndesugared for now:\r\n \r\n```\r\n1.  If condition, then let |result| be `\"foo\"`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich is in fact sugar for:\r\n\r\n```\r\n1.  If condition, then:\r\n    1.  let |result| be `\"foo\"`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nBlocks in loops are  the only ones which need to take initial key/value pairs (usually each item of the list that's being looped over) and be explicitly constructed. For example, for \"For each\":\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<p>To <dfn export for=list,set lt=\"iterate|for each\">iterate</dfn> over a <a>list</a>, performing a\r\nset of steps on each <a for=list>item</a> in order, use phrasing of the form\r\n\"<a for=list>For each</a> |item| of <var ignore>list</var>\", and then operate on |item| in the\r\nsubsequent prose.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe should add something like:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<p><a for=list>For each</a> creates a new <a>block</a> for each <a>item</a> in <a>list</a>,\r\nwith its <a>initial variable</a> \"item\" set to the corresponding <a>item</a>.\r\n```\r\nSo we'd have to add a definition of _block_, _initial variable_, and _desugared_ step.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
