    "body": "> Ideally step 4 doesn't have access to i, right?\r\n\r\nAh, yes, Infra looping constructs should create blocks on their own.  (We don't want Python-style visibility of the final iteration's variable bindings to later steps.)\r\n\r\n> Conditional statements which occur in the same step are—I think—the only ones which need to be desugared for now:\r\n\r\nI don't think this is correct; I think you'll usually want |foo| to be visible to step 2 of that algorithm, not be scoped to just that item.",
