    "body": "I don't think that's particularly error-prone; presumably there will be more steps in the inner list.  If you want that variables exposed in the outer list, you'll define it in a previous step, then use `set` in the inner list to update the value.  And with the scoping rules in place, it'll be obvious when you mess up. (If you refer to the definition outside the inner list, it'll complain; if you use `let` in the inner list *and* the outer list, it'll complain.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
