    "updated_at": "2018-06-08T22:56:19Z",
    "body": "Yes, I don't think we need to do anything special for \"if\" statements.\r\n\r\nThat code example should be fine - the step 3 |foo| is referencing the |foo| defined in step 2.  The fact that |foo| is undefined if |condition| is false is a spec bug, that's all.\r\n\r\n(I can see the argument for making \"if\" a scoping block, but I can't auto-detect that since conditionals aren't Infra constructs.)",
