    "body": "Hmm, I see what you mean.\r\n\r\nIs this intent here to prevent shadowing, or to prevent any kind of reuse?\r\n\r\nWhen writing JS, some folks don't like shadowing, but I don't think folks are against reuse:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst links = [...document.querySelectorAll('a[href]')];\r\nconst crossOriginLinks = links.map(a => new URL(a.href).origin === location.origin);\r\nconst httpLinks = links.map(a => new URL(a.href).protocol === 'http:');\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't think the reuse of `a` is generally seen as bad.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
